# Drift Bot

Telegram repo-monitoring agent. Users connect GitHub repos; Drift Bot runs cheap daily checks (dependency drift, CVEs, framework-relevant changes) and optional LLM deep research. Results go back as Telegram messages.

## Current phase

Billing plus public-repo audits in a pnpm + Turborepo monorepo. Users get a 30-day Paid trial on first `/start`, then monthly Telegram Stars subscriptions (`/tier`, `/upgrade`). They connect **public** GitHub repos with `/connect owner/repo` and run `/audit_secrets`, `/audit_deps`, `/audit_code`, `/audit_contracts`, and `/audit` (Break before launch). Do not add the GitHub App, scheduler, or LLM deep research until asked.

## Billing

- New users get Paid limits for 30 days (`trial_ends_at`). After that they drop to Free unless a Stars subscription is active.
- Checkout is Telegram Stars (`XTR`, 30-day `subscription_period`). Users can pay Stars from Telegram Wallet. Do not add Stripe or TON Connect unless asked.
- Enforce free / paid / premium limits in the API against `usage_counters` and `resolveAccess`, not only in bot UX.
- The API is the only process that talks to Postgres. The bot is stateless and resolves accounts from `telegram_user_id` via the API (`INTERNAL_API_SECRET`).

## Layout

`apps/bot`, `apps/api`, `apps/worker`; `packages/{db,types,github-client,stack-detector,registry-clients,audit-engine,llm-engine}`. `packages/db` stays **Prisma** (not Drizzle).

## Live GitHub checks

What we offer on a connected repo is `docs/audit-checklist.md` / `packages/audit-engine/src/catalog.ts`.

MVP live now: `/audit_secrets` (pattern scan), `/audit_deps` (OSV CVEs), `/audit_code` (risky-pattern SAST), `/audit_contracts` (Solidity footguns, if `.sol` files). `/audit` (**Break before launch**) runs all of those and asks the user to fix every P0. External CLIs (Gitleaks, Semgrep, Slither) and the LLM wrap can replace these later.

Solana contract audit is a stub in `packages/audit-engine/src/contracts/solana/` (v2). Public repos only until the GitHub App ships.

## Planned deep research

`/changelog`, `/migrate`, `/compat`, `/ask` — catalog in `packages/llm-engine/src/operations.ts`.

## Stack

Node.js, TypeScript, grammY, Fastify, Prisma, Postgres, pnpm, Turborepo.
